# Build output
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# Visual Studio
.vs/
*.VC.db
*.VC.opendb

# NuGet
packages/
*.nupkg

# Runtime artifacts produced next to the executable.
# The atomic writers create these as <file>.tmp / <file>.bak; a leftover one means a save was
# interrupted, so do not commit them - but do not delete them either, they may be a
# recoverable copy of a user's data file.
*.tmp
*.bak

# User data. These are the files the app reads and writes at runtime, and several are very
# large; they are not source.
#   Config.xml   - colour theme
#   Options.xml  - language, sort order, image folder
#   Events.xml   - banner events
#   *.xml at the repo root are exported folder trees (one is ~150 MB)

# Note: the checked-in copies of Config.xml / Options.xml / Events.xml under the project root
# are intentionally tracked - they are the defaults the app copies to its output directory.
# Only ignore them once the project has been switched to a per-user location.

# Large exported folder-tree data files (not source)
/Drive G4.xml
/soft.xml
